<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Delville Wood</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Delville Wood was fought from 15 July to 3 September 1916 as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-somme">Battle of the Somme</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The 1st South African Infantry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">Brigade</a> was ordered to take the wood and hold it at all costs, and clung on for six days under intense German shelling and counter-attacks; of more than 3,000 men who went in, only about 750 came out unhurt. The South African National Memorial now stands there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-delville-wood.jpg" alt="Battle of Delville Wood" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG version, and changes: Grandiose Original map:Worldwari map13 largerview.jpg, US Military Inset map: Giro720, File... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Battle_of_the_Somme,_1916.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
